This PR adds a smoke test to assert that the frontend assets of the elasticsearch decoupled datasource have been built and load.Note: I am actually not sure that elastic search has been decoupled but this shouldn't hurt anything :sSee https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/94977 for additional context | This PR adds a smoke test to assert that the frontend assets of the cloudwatch decoupled datasource have been built and load.See https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/94977 for additional context  | Update plugin.json keywords to include "datasource" + "database"Related to https://github.com/grafana/oss-plugin-partnerships/issues/1055 | Backport d817ee9b99bd1b46a0a93ede9fc85e37fbf1ba77 from #91823---Follow up on https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/88963Add concrete example to docs and imageNote: I think this PR should be backported to v11.2.x but that tag doesn't seem to be created yet 🤔 <img width="433" alt="Screenshot 2024-08-12 at 7 50 34 PM" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/01855a1a-0344-4eec-8117-b708e82e7af3"> | Backport 787abccfbc9e16b68b3295b17269cb3b46b88527 from #91654---Fixes issue where selecto selection box would be drawn when moving certain newly added elements to the canvas. This issue was impacting: - `Ellipse`- `Server`- `Triangle`- `Cloud`- `Parallelogram`- `Button`- `Wind turbine`- `All drone elements`Beforehttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/95f5fd71-8178-4b17-accb-9dcafd882475Afterhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/718f99ff-f298-40b3-bfaa-8bc10e8b408aThe way we were calculating whether or not a element was already selected was contingent on having a consistent DOM structure which is no longer the case.Fixes https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/91558 | Follow up on https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/88963Add concrete example to docs and imageNote: I think this PR should be backported to v11.2.x but that tag doesn't seem to be created yet 🤔 <img width="433" alt="Screenshot 2024-08-12 at 7 50 34 PM" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/01855a1a-0344-4eec-8117-b708e82e7af3"> | Before key value were appearing seemingly backwards in select list (showing keys instead of values and persisting this backwards. Maybe I am wrong though 🤷‍♂️ Before![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cda32b74-a46d-4709-9e3e-19da3767a884)After![Screenshot 2024-08-09 at 12 15 20 AM](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6c518ddb-82de-4b7f-a8c8-d426d608c7c5) | Fixes issue where selecto selection box would be drawn when moving certain newly added elements to the canvas. This issue was impacting: - `Ellipse`- `Server`- `Triangle`- `Cloud`- `Parallelogram`- `Button`- `Wind turbine`- `All drone elements`Beforehttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/95f5fd71-8178-4b17-accb-9dcafd882475Afterhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/718f99ff-f298-40b3-bfaa-8bc10e8b408aThe way we were calculating whether or not a element was already selected was contingent on having a consistent DOM structure which is no longer the case.Fixes https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/91558 | During selection of elements for ad-hoc viz creation, after creation of the ad-hoc viz, dragging the new viz element behaves strangely. I think we need to unselect after creation of ad-hoc viz.https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fef8868e-fd0c-4cfd-92f9-289745d1ce0e | @nmarrs add context here.This also covers the strategy for handling interoperability between elements. | Promote XYChart to generally available for OSS / onPrem Grafana. We have performed a gradual rollout of XYChart in Grafana Cloud and are confident with releasing XYChart as generally available for OSS / onPrem builds. | Support variable interpolation for the base URL in a canvas action. Beforehttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/575f92a7-8eb5-4009-be0f-0df68b1dafe3After (note the CORS issue but the request is going through)https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f6059709-020f-442b-b9c9-a0b36577bd49 | Promote the format string transformation as generally available. This will enable users to try out this transformation.[Related cloud rollout PR](https://github.com/grafana/deployment_tools/pull/160583) | Promote the add field from calc stat function transformation as generally available. The transformation itself was actually already available, but this enables the cumulative and window functions. This will enable users to try out these calculation options in this transformation.[Related cloud rollout PR](https://github.com/grafana/deployment_tools/pull/160581) | Add support for template variable interpolation for the regex matcher.Beforehttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/27331226-fa5d-4b34-b2b3-d5096187cf44After https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/967ea5ff-b07a-4d29-b52d-4d7731a7249c[Filter by value transformation regex variable support-1721896735727.json](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/16373088/Filter.by.value.transformation.regex.variable.support-1721896735727.json)Fixes https://github.com/grafana/support-escalations/issues/11615 | It [was recently reported](https://raintank-corp.slack.com/archives/C065F70N2Q7/p1721294072963189) that cell units were prepending vs appending the values in table cells.It turns out this was a regression caused by [this PR](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/90353)This PR implements a quick fix to handle the case when the cell's field has a unit set.Before<img width="801" alt="Screenshot 2024-07-22 at 2 59 29 PM" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/120ad967-a35c-403a-abc6-0dd646f693d5">After<img width="796" alt="Screenshot 2024-07-22 at 2 59 07 PM" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1bf14a33-c505-47f1-9c70-f04ece6291d9">Repro dashboard[debug-Panel Title-2024-07-22 15_02_28.json.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/16340149/debug-Panel.Title-2024-07-22.15_02_28.json.txt) | <img width="261" alt="Screenshot 2024-07-15 at 9 30 29 PM" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d6ac9fa7-72e2-41c7-bb17-551598f52f94"> | Rough WIPWhile implementing this it occurred to me that perhaps we do not need to support one-click datalink functionality for table as it currently already has support (provided you add a single data link). Even for the data link cell type each link is accessible via a single click...Similar concept for panels such as piechart that also have "one-click" capability already enabledDigging into this code though it is apparent that there will be some challenges in adding support to other panels as it will most likely mean modifying the shared data link editor that is shared across all visualizations<img width="1340" alt="Screenshot 2024-07-12 at 5 35 48 PM" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/029047c2-4bab-4c05-becc-adbc6b9447a1"> | Add support for one click data link functionality in tableIn the case of table there already is existing one click functionality when a single data link exists. However if there are multiple data links a context menu is opened so the initial version of this will be to handle this casehttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a5dc9286-3feb-4b4e-aa2e-eb18ba7d8b77 | Promote the group to nested table transformation as generally available. This will enable users to try out this transformation.Note: The "beta" label was added to denote that there might be some lingering bugs given the low amount of usage of the transformation so far (due to being behind feature toggle). This beta label does not denote the feature's availability (which is GA as of 11.2) - confusing.. yes 😬 ![Screenshot 2024-07-09 at 4 36 50 PM](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/22381771/ee38361d-6a9c-4dfe-8445-2b6587b86108)[Related cloud rollout PR](https://github.com/grafana/deployment_tools/pull/155211) | Follow-up from https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/89852 | Update GitHub automation for DataViz squad- Add table to dataviz project instead of deprecated BI- Remove add to project commands from `pr-commands.json` as they were not working as expected and instead only include them in `commands.json` file- Remove icon panel reference as [this alpha panel was removed a while back](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/68573)Note: Will create a follow-up PR linting these files as there are a number of styling issues | Noticed that the element item in the editor list was not centered 🙃Before<img width="371" alt="before" src="https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/22381771/d8e5b9b5-a799-43b1-a8c6-42729f14dd1b">After<img width="376" alt="after" src="https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/22381771/82fed66d-fefb-48e6-8ecc-f4f63ed48e4e"> | Canvas code has built up some technical debt over the years and some files have become unruly and difficult to manage. The purpose of this epic is to pay down this technical debt, improve our understanding of canvas code, improve maintainability and more.```[tasklist]### Tasks- [ ] https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/87477- [ ] https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/88010- [ ] https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/88491- [ ] https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/88517- [ ] Resolve duplicate typescript object issue (i.e. two CanvasElementOptions definitions, two CanvasConnection definitions etc)- [ ] Refactor / break up ConnectionSVG.tsx file- [ ] Refactor / break up Connection.tsx file- [ ] Refactor / break up element.tsx file- [ ] Refactor / remove basic utils.ts file (not a huge fan of a generic utils file, we can move functions to domain area (i.e. connection calcs can go to connections code area etc)- [ ] Finish cleaning up canvas betterer issues (missing <Trans> wrappers for text)``` | This has been on my radar for a very long time. This refactors the `scene.tsx` file to be more manageable and easier to understand.The main way this has been accomplished is by moving related logic for element management and "ables" management into two separate files.This refactor is by no means perfect, but I think gets us closer to a better, more maintainable state.Note: This PR should be rebased / merged after [this other clean up PR](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/88491) is mergedThere are a number of other refactors / files that I noted as part of this initial push, I will create a small epic soon (TODO) to capture these so others can join in the fun ;)  | Fix the last remaining betterer issues in the canvas visualization code... well that didn't last long 🙃, there [are more betterer issues to address for canvas now](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/88479) lolContinuation of [efforts from before](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/88010) :) | Update docs to account for [newly added color options for percent change](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/88205)<img width="801" alt="docs update" src="https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/22381771/6923edd2-3f60-46b2-907c-61b69e153ebc"> | Clean up almost all of the remaining betterer issuesThe last two files / betterer issues will require a bit more extensive refactor that I will follow-up with to get rid of canvas's [barrel files](https://uglow.medium.com/burn-the-barrel-c282578f21b6)Related to https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/87477 | We want to enable one click data link access universally in Grafana.What this will look like is a setting that a user can toggle that enables the user to access the first data link in a visualization via a single click. [See this initial attempt at implementing this only for the canvas panel for reference](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/85430).Fixes https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/79698Fixes https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/77246Fixes https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/79479 | Adhere canvas editing state to dashboard's editable state. Before if the dashboard was read-only, users could still modify the canvas but would then have no way to save those changes.Note: this approach will need to be updated for dashboard scene migration, but given as that is currently in public preview it makes sense to fix classic dashboards for the time beingSee [this follow up GitHub issue](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/87948)Beforehttps://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/9974811/81921431-57e5-461d-825b-25bc91d1366fAfterhttps://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/22381771/155ee8a3-c7b4-435d-be07-a22a064b8746Fixes https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/87446 | Add string type check for field value for the substring value matcher. Field values are not always strings and can be arrays etc. We will now return false if the value passed is not a string and causing a runtime error<img width="520" alt="Screenshot 2024-05-13 at 4 31 20 PM" src="https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/22381771/9a336fdd-f5a2-425d-a9f6-e7ffe2d20faa">See [this thread in slack](https://raintank-corp.slack.com/archives/C04J73AAQ87/p1715628397081029) for additional context | Fix description of infinite panning editor option as it was missing a word | Clean up canvas betterer complaints. For a good amount waived away betterer warnings for battle tested code but fixed / addressed some issues.Main reason behind these changes is to reduce risk of future cleanup refactors from breaking critical functionality which occurred recently with https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/87363Did not address all canvas betterer issues, the last two files will require a bit more extensive refactor that I will follow-up with to get rid of canvas's [barrel files](https://uglow.medium.com/burn-the-barrel-c282578f21b6)  | ### What happened?https://github.com/grafana/grafana/assets/9974811/81921431-57e5-461d-825b-25bc91d1366fIt looks like even though making a dashboard "read-only" should disable all editing on a dashboard, inline-edits for canvas panels still work - even though the changes cannot be saved.### What did you expect to happen?I would expect inline-editing to be disabled if a dashboard is set to read-only.### Did this work before?I am not sure it worked before.### How do we reproduce it?1. Open a dashboard with a Canvas panel on it2. Enable inline editing for the Canvas panel3. Make the dashboard read-only under Settings4. Reload the page5. Check if inline edit still works### Is the bug inside a dashboard panel?| Key | Value ||--|--|| Panel | canvas @ 11.1.0-70397 || Grafana | Grafana v11.1.0-70397 (0c702d335e) // Cloud Pro |<details><summary>Panel debug snapshot dashboard</summary>```json{  "panels": [    {      "datasource": {        "type": "grafana",        "uid": "grafana"      },      "fieldConfig": {        "defaults": {          "mappings": [],          "thresholds": {            "mode": "absolute",            "steps": [              {                "color": "green",                "value": null              },              {                "color": "red",                "value": 80              }            ]          },          "color": {            "mode": "thresholds"          }        },        "overrides": []      },      "gridPos": {        "h": 13,        "w": 15,        "x": 0,        "y": 0      },      "id": 2,      "options": {        "inlineEditing": true,        "showAdvancedTypes": true,        "panZoom": false,        "infinitePan": false,        "root": {          "background": {            "color": {              "fixed": "transparent"            }          },          "border": {            "color": {              "fixed": "dark-green"            }          },          "elements": [            {              "background": {                "color": {                  "fixed": "#D9D9D9"                }              },              "border": {                "color": {                  "fixed": "dark-green"                }              },              "config": {                "align": "center",                "color": {                  "fixed": "#000000"                },                "size": 20,                "text": {                  "field": "",                  "fixed": "",                  "mod